libtheora 1.2.0, decoder only, for the UC2 movie player (Source/UC2Movie, milestone M9).

Source: the official Xiph.Org release tarball
  https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/theora/libtheora-1.2.0.tar.xz
  SHA-256 ebdf77a8f5c0a8f7a9e42323844fa09502b34eb1d1fece7b5f54da41fe2122ec
  (matches https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/theora/SHA256SUMS), fetched 2026-10-04.

Copied byte for byte, nothing edited:
  include/theora/codec.h, theoradec.h, theora.h (lib/internal.h includes theora.h)
  lib/: the decoder sources of lib/Makefile.am's decoder_sources without the legacy theora_* API wrapper
        (apiwrapper.c, decapiwrapper.c, apiwrapper.h) and without the x86/ARM/C64x assembly:
        bitpack decinfo decode dequant fragment huffdec idct info internal quant state (.c and their .h),
        plus dct.h decint.h huffman.h modedec.h ocintrin.h
  COPYING, LICENSE, AUTHORS, README.md

Ours: CMakeLists.txt (static library `theora`, links the vendored libogg) and this file. Neither OC_X86_ASM nor
OC_ARM_ASM is defined, so the plain C paths are built on every target (32-bit native, MinGW, Emscripten).
The vendored libogg is 1.0, which lacks ogg_uint16_t and ogg_uint64_t: CMakeLists.txt defines both as
macros for this library and everything that links it.
